From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:06:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 66/74] pwm: Add Ingenic X2600 PWM driver

Add a driver for the 16-channel PWM controller of the Ingenic X2600,
using the waveform callbacks. Each channel counts a high and a low phase
of up to 65535 ticks of its prescaled clock (1 to 65536); INL picks the
phase a period starts with, which gives the duty offsets 0 and
period - duty, and IDL the level a stopped channel rests at, which gives
the 0% and 100% duty cycles the counters can't produce.

The behaviour the driver relies on was measured on an X2600 (a
Flashforge Adventurer 5X), Ingenic's SDK driver being the only other
reference: the counts and INL of a running channel are shadowed until
UPT and the end of the period, the prescaler is not, and stopping a
channel finishes the phase in progress first. The DMA modes and the
capture unit are not supported.
